 - Import form (`imports/new.html.erb`): `form_with url: moderate_import_path, local: true`, `<label for="quiz_json">Quiz JSON</label>` + `<textarea id="quiz_json" name="quiz_json" aria-label="Quiz JSON" placeholder="Quiz JSON">` (no `required` so empty reaches server and shows error), `<button>Import</button>`. Errors in `.errors` list, status 422, preserves `@quiz_json`.
 - Import logic (`ImportsController#create`): `JSON.parse(params[:quiz_json])` → `Invalid JSON` on parse error; requires Hash, `title` String non-blank else `Title can't be blank`, `questions` Array else `Questions must be an array`. Per question: `text` String non-blank else `Question N: Question can't be blank` (same phrase as form), `active` optional bool default true else `Active must be true or false`, `options` Array else `Add at least two options`; each option `text` String stripped (non-string/nil → blank filtered), `correct` optional bool default false else error. Then same as form: filter blanks, `<2` → `Question N: Add at least two options`, none correct → `Question N: Mark at least one option as correct`. Extra keys ignored. Validates all before DB write; creates in transaction (`Quiz.create!` + `questions.create!(position: idx+1)` + `options.create!(position)`) so nothing partial. Always new quiz (no uniqueness). Redirects to `moderate_quiz_path(new_quiz)`.
 - Verified: integration tests for valid/defaults/order/duplicate/roundtrip/HTML-escape/empty/missing/invalid, Capybara rack_test `click_on "Import quiz"`, `fill_in "Quiz JSON"`, `click_on "Import"`, `click_on "Export"`, single `<pre>` parses, invalid shows `Invalid JSON` 422, production curl via `bin/rails server` (Basic auth + CSRF) 302 on valid, 422 on invalid.
+
+## Live Game (2026-10-07)
+- Gems: `rqrcode ~> 3.2` for QR SVG (local, no external). `cuprite` in test group for browser live tests (Ferrum + /usr/bin/chromium, no chromedriver needed).
+- Data: `Game(quiz_id, code[5 upper alnum unique], status: waiting/open/closed/ended, current_question_id?)`, `Player(game_id, name, token[hex unique])`, `Answer(game_id, player_id, question_id, option_id, unique [player,question])`. Live active list (`where(active:true).order(position,id)`) so games skip inactive even if toggled mid-game; `current_question_id` + `next_active_after` avoids index shifts. `with_lock` for start/finish/advance/end.
+- Routes: `POST /moderate/quizzes/:quiz_id/games` (Start a game → redirect to big-screen), `GET .../games/:id` (big-screen), `POST .../start|finish|next_step|end_quiz`, `GET .../state.json` (moderator poll, Basic auth). `GET /play/:code` (join or game, no auth, case-insensitive), `POST /play/:code/join`, `POST /play/:code/answer`, `GET /play/:code/state.json` (player poll via cookie).
+- Moderator big-screen (`games/show`): waiting shows quiz title, join URL (`request.base_url/play/CODE` with scheme, same string in QR via `RQRCode::QRCode.new(url).as_svg`), `#qr-code svg`, `Players: N`, Start button. Open shows `Question N of T`, body, `<ol><li stage-option>` without counts/Correct, `Players: N` + `Answers: A / N`, Finish. Closed shows counts per option (`stage-option__count`) + `Correct` marking (`is-correct` + bar), Next or End quiz (last). Ended shows `The quiz is over`. Quiz page added `Start a game` (button_to POST).
+- Player (`play/show_*`): join form has `<label>Your name` + input placeholder/aria-label + Join button; after join `Hi, <name>!` + waiting. Cookie `quizzy_player_CODE=token` (1yr, httponly, lax, /) remembers; `current_player` prefers `params[:token]` (for tests) then cookie, scoped to game. Join allowed in waiting/open/closed, blocked when ended (shows over, no Join). Open shows question + options as `<button>` in forms (fallback) with `Your answer` marking for picked, changeable until closed (find_or_initialize, last wins, ignored when not open). Closed shows `Correct!`/`Wrong!`/`No answer` via server-computed `result_text` + `result_class` (right/wrong/neutral). Ended shows over.
+- No leak: player JSON (`joined,game_status,quiz_title,total,num,progress,is_over,player_name,greeting,question_id,question_body,options[id,text,letter,picked],result_text,result_class,can_answer`) has no key containing forbidden substring; when open `result_text=nil`, no counts/correct. Player HTML/JS when open has no `correct` substring (verified via `grep -i`): JS uses server `result_text`/`result_class` directly, no hardcoded Correct!, no `is-correct`, no comments with forbidden word. Moderator JSON (auth) includes `correct`+counts, UI hides until closed.
+- Live (crowded wifi): vanilla `fetch` polling every 500ms, `credentials:same-origin`, `Accept:json`, `X-CSRF-Token` for POSTs, `catch`+retry, `visibilitychange`+`document.hidden` guard, no ActionCable/Redis. Moderator JS updates `Players:`/`Answers:`/`count-N` in place without reload (reload only on state change from other tab or after own action POST). Player JS (`show_player`) fully re-renders greeting/waiting/question/options/result/over from JSON without reload; `show_join` polls for `is_over` to flip to over. Answer POST via fetch without reload (fallback to normal submit on network fail).
+- Verified: `test/integration/game_live_test.rb` (full flow, skip inactive, change answer, counts, Correct!/Wrong!/No answer, late join, over, isolation, no-leak checks), `game_edge_test.rb` (empty/all-inactive→ended, single→End quiz, multi-correct 2×Correct, join during open/closed, ignore when closed, auth, case-insensitive, escaping/blank), `test/system/live_game_test.rb` (Cuprite/Chromium multi-session live: join→Players live, Start→Q live, answer→Answers live, Finish→Correct!/Wrong! live, late No answer, Next/End→over live, no Join after end, no leak). Production verified via `bin/rails server` + Cuprite remote (CSRF/Basic OK, join URL host correct) and `bin/serve` (db:prepare, assets, 0.0.0.0:PORT, /up 200, any host, plain HTTP, storage/production.sqlite3, /quizzy.css 200).
